{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788227667,"nonce":"d4hzWumBx8OWALhoKx9JqdvWqpY=","message":"GREEN — closed on live acceptance, session 11 (`65b03c2`), 2026-08-31. The last outstanding bullet is now proven.\n\n\nAcceptance bullet 2 required more than a flipped flag: \"`unforbid` over the kit's rect clears it, **and a pawn then picks the gear up** — proving the obstacle was real and the remedy works, not just that a flag flipped.\"\n\nA first attempt failed to show it: after unforbidding the kit and advancing 12,000 ticks, nothing moved, and two colonists sat \"wandering\" while the gear lay on the ground. Work priorities were checked and ruled out — `Hauling` is priority 3 on the colonist read.\n\n**The cause was the fixture, and it is worth recording because it will mislead the next person too.** `zones` reports Stockpile zone 1 at `[108,127]` with **144 cells**, filter allowing Apparel and Weapons. `dev:starter-kit` places at the colony anchor, `[112,128]`–`[114,133]` — **inside that zone.** The gear was already in valid storage, so not hauling was CORRECT behaviour. There was nothing to haul.\n\nShown properly by spawning outside every zone:\n\n```\ndev:spawn-thing {def: Apparel_Parka, stuff: Cloth, pos: [126,120], forbid: true}\n  -\u003e placed at [126,120], forbidden: true\nunforbid {rect: [125,119,3,3]}\nadvance {ticks: 3000}\n  -\u003e parka 26816 now at [136,134], forbidden: false\n```\n\n`[136,134]` is Stockpile zone 2. **A colonist picked it up and hauled it.** The obstacle was real, the remedy worked, and the pickup happened — all three, measured.\n\nThis also exercises the new opt-in `forbid` arg on `dev:spawn-thing` (default `false`), which is how the kit reuses placement rather than reimplementing it.\n\n\n- **The kit lands forbidden**: `forbidden_stacks: 10`, `not_forbiddable: []`.\n- **Confirmed by a second, independent verb**: `unforbid` over the kit's rect accepted exactly **10** — `Designator_Unforbid.CanDesignateThing` only accepts a genuinely forbidden thing, so that count is the game's answer, not ours. A second `unforbid` accepted **0**, all cells `not-designatable`.\n- **The obstacle persists**: left forbidden and advanced 2,500 ticks, all 10 stacks were still there and still forbidden.\n- **Journaled as a dev action**: row `type: dev`, seq 133, payload carrying `forbid: true`, `forbidden_stacks: 10`, `not_forbiddable: 0` and the plan — so M1's no-dev-verbs-after-staging invariant reads off the journal alone.\n- **The other staging verbs are decided and stated**: `dev:spawn-thing` does NOT follow by default (its provenance is `DebugThingPlaceHelper.DebugSpawn`, which forbids nothing — a bare spawn models a thing APPEARING, an arrival is a different fiction); `dev:spawn-pawn`, `dev:finish-research` and `dev:unfog` have nothing to forbid.\n\n\nBecause the kit lands inside the existing stockpile on the bench save, **M1 will not rehearse `unforbid`-then-haul unless the kit is placed away from storage** — the whole point of this issue. Whoever stages M1 should either place the kit outside the stockpile or accept that the rehearsal is not exercised, and say which.","files":null}]}